{"_id":"6a2ff5062204ffbc59e5a5c0","roadmapSlug":"python-data-analysis","nodeId":"Rq9TFEEJnjEgVa1DiJxFz","description":"# Merging & Joining\n\nPandas provides `merge()` and `join()` for combining DataFrames based on common columns or indices. Merge supports inner, left, right, and outer joins, mirroring SQL JOIN behavior. `concat()` stacks DataFrames vertically or horizontally. These operations are used to combine data from multiple sources into a single analysis-ready table.","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Merge, join, concatenate and compare","url":"https://pandas.pydata.org/docs/user_guide/merging.html","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb23"},{"type":"article","title":"Combining Data in pandas With merge(), .join(), and concat()","url":"https://realpython.com/pandas-merge-join-and-concat/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb24"},{"type":"article","title":"Pandas: Combining Data","url":"https://towardsdatascience.com/pandas-combining-data-b190d793b626/","_id":"6a75d326b0650226a50aeb25"}],"createdAt":"2026-06-15T12:50:14.357Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:22.099Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e3360acf8c05faf5e1c2a","title":"DataCamp - Data Analyst with Python","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/QY0dY9"},{"_id":"6a5e3365acf8c05faf5e1ded","title":"DataCamp - Python Data Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/k4V24x"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python-data-analysis/content/Rq9TFEEJnjEgVa1DiJxFz.md"}